# Changelog
## [1.0.0-rc1] - 2026-11-11
### Breaking changes
 - API break: Drop Clone for Socket. (c71db75)
 - Bump MSRV to 1.85 and edition to 2024. (32bede1)
 - Remove constants module and inline constants. (3636648)
 - API break: replace bytes::BufMut with &mut [u8]. (156c1f5)
 - Stop exposing netlink constants. (78a3f3a)

### New features
 - Add support for FreeBSD. (ca4318a 1ee3a02 41f6448 067aa20)

### Bug fixes
 - async: fix send_to doc comment. (038da26)
 - tokio: return an error when no runtime is available. (7599ad6)
 - async: make socket_mut unsafe. (9e6b02c)
 - socket: use socklen_t for recvfrom address length. (0159d87)
 - socket: pass an int-sized value to SO_RCVBUF. (d98f740)
 - socket: reject out-of-range protocols and gate big-endian doctests. (7136122)
 - socket: retry interrupted syscalls. (725760b)
 - socket: ignore EINPROGRESS on connect. (f21c324)
 - Add SAFETY comments to unsafe blocks. (3053f37)
 - examples: fix stale docs and use error returns. (71a0fdc)
 - docs: fix SocketAddr docs and Display. (0f32535)
 - deps: remove futures-util. (115bc25)
 - smol: drop redundant set_nonblocking call. (158df9e)
 - fix: match name with the std's & socket2's `set_nonblocking`. (c9aaa23)
 - tokio: use AsyncFd::register. (6ff6960)
 - Document raw fd and socket_mut safety. (2d71a86)
 - set_rx_buf_sz: take usize and pass it through. (307fbd9)
 - Make Socket::bind and bind_auto take &self. (8aa8cca)
 - Document all public APIs. (b78dbaa)
 - Fix panics on unexpected lengths from the kernel. (8899edc)
 - LICENSE: fix LICENSE-MIT. (2a27adb)

## [0.9.0] - 2026-08-18
### Breaking changes
 - Use netlink-packet-core 0.9.0. (5dd7b8e)

### New features
 - Implement IntoRawFd for Socket. (0d3bf1d)

### Bug fixes
 - make testsuite pass on bigendian. (600033d)
 - fix: build rust docs for all features, so that we can see `TokioSocket` and
   others in docs.rs.. (3a49d41)
 - CHANGELOG: Use `-` instead of `*` for aligning with other rust-netlink
   crates. (5c08a3a)

